Note on scope, stated plainly: copyright protects the code and the written
material, not an abstract idea. What this licence does control is copying the
implementation, redistributing builds, and reusing the source to make another
product. That is what the restrictions above enforce.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TWO BUILDS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source supports two configurations:

  PERSONAL / FREE BUILD
      RAVE variant engine compiled in. Free to use and share. May not be
      sold, because the RAVE code and weights are CC-BY-NC 4.0.

  COMMERCIAL BUILD
      Compiled with -DBTP_ENABLE_RAVE=OFF and packaged with -NoRave. Contains
      no non-commercial components. This is the only configuration covered
      by a JUCE commercial licence and the only one that may be sold.

Only BtP may produce and sell the commercial build. Building it yourself from
this source does not grant you the right to distribute or sell it.

See Packaging/BUILD-VARIANTS.txt and Packaging/LICENSING.txt.

